xodus-service: answer the game's Store questions (licence tokens, its own licence, the Store catalog, account roles)

MetalHorizon 1.0.4. The engines run Ferestre's xgameruntime (icex/xgameruntime), which asks the service for Store
licence tokens (XML message type 7, XStoreQueryLicenseTokenAsync), the game's own licence (ESDX frames), the Store
catalog (CSDX frames) and the account roles (ASDX frames). This service, from upstream xodus with MetalHorizon's
patches 0002 to 0004, knew none of them: "Unimplemented" and "Unknown magic" in its log, a closed connection for the
game, and in the game no VIP membership, no Car Pass cars and no expansions (MetalHorizon issue #18).

- connection/license.rs: licence tokens the way Ferestre's service (icex/xodus a4f9d5c) asks them, POST
  /v8.0/licenseToken authorized and signed with the title's XSTS token for licensing.mp.microsoft.com, through the
  service's existing XSTS path (xml.rs: xsts_response, factored out of the XSTS branch). Bound to the game's Store ID
  (XODUS_STORE_PRODUCT, binding.rs) when the launcher passes it.
- connection/catalog.rs: Ferestre's Store catalog bridge, unchanged (plus one live test, ignored by default).
- connection/router.rs: the three frames above; a client closing its connection is no longer logged as an error.
- xml.rs: the runtime's extended frame size (type bit 0x8000) for requests over 64 KiB; any XML type is answered with
  its type plus one, as the runtime checks.
- proto.rs: the unimplemented protobuf framing refuses instead of panicking.
- main.rs: --latest-version <content id>, the version Microsoft publishes for the game's package (authenticated package
  service, http://update.xboxlive.com), so MetalHorizon can offer an update to an outdated game.
- device.rs: when Microsoft's ticket exchange refuses, the device ticket is renewed once from the stored device key
  (as Ferestre does since icex/xodus e35bde1) and the request tried again, in the service and in --check; the renewed
  ticket stays in memory (nothing written to the Keychain).

